# Druid — a Weak enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 1/12 Weak enemies — 10 life, bribe 40 gold
# enemy: Druid (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0139.dck "Druid (G, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3 file
#   dated 2016-02-15; its first 16 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 13 lines (60 cards)
#   after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its .vNone/.v<Colour>
#   sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/druid.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 1) [Tier 3
#   — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/druid.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Weak) — "Druid" (Original) [Tier-web
#   — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Druid
20 Forest
4 Mishra's Factory
3 Ley Druid
3 Llanowar Elves
2 Oasis
3 Wooden Sphere
4 Giant Growth
3 Wanderlust
2 Wall of Wood
2 Nafs Asp
2 Giant Spider
2 Craw Wurm
2 Ironroot Treefolk
3 Instill Energy
2 Killer Bees
2 Durkwood Boars
3 Grizzly Bears
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Grizzly Bears
#   .vBlack  3 Grizzly Bears
#   .vBlue   3 Grizzly Bears
#   .vGreen  3 Shanodin Dryads
#   .vRed    3 Grizzly Bears
#   .vWhite  3 Grizzly Bears
SB: 3 Shanodin Dryads
